Mastering DevOps Repositories – A Quick Summary Table for Every Engineer! 🔧

In the world of DevOps, managing code, packages, containers, and secrets efficiently is key to delivering reliable software at scale. Here's a summary table that breaks down the essential types of repositories, popular tools, and who typically uses them:

🔹 Source Code Repo – GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket
👨💻 Used by: Devs, DevOps

🔹 Artifact Repo – Nexus, Artifactory, PyPI, npm
⚙️ Used by: Devs, DevOps

🔹 Container Repo – Docker Hub, ECR, GCR
🐳 Used by: DevOps, SREs

🔹 Config/IaC Repo – Terraform, Ansible, Helm
🛠️ Used by: DevOps, Cloud Engineers

🔹 OS Package Repo – YUM, APT, Zypper
🧑💻 Used by: SysAdmins

🔹 Large File Repo – S3, Azure Blob, GCS
📦 Used by: DevOps, ML Engineers

🔹 Helm Chart Repo – ArtifactHub, Harbor
☸️ Used by: Kubernetes Engineers

🔹 Secret Management Repo – Vault, Secrets Manager
🔐 Used by: DevOps, Security
